WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:03.880
Hey Crazies.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:07.820
There’s this thing that teachers like to
say in introductory physics courses:

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.460
Magnetic force cannot do work.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:14.140
But this is the Science Asylum and we can’t
ever forget Rule #8:

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:15.940
Question Everything!

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:19.360
Before we get into magnets though, let’s
start with a more fundamental question:

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:20.540
What is work?

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.440
Well, you can’t really define work without
also defining energy.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:27.300
Yes, I’ve covered energy before… in several
videos.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.980
Here’s a summary of what we know so far:
Energy isn’t anything by itself.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.120
It’s just a number.

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:37.200
We assign this number to actual things like
planets, people, or particles.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.940
The specific value of that number doesn’t
matter.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:44.780
Whatever number that is, as long as there
is symmetry across time, the total number

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:45.790
never changes.

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:47.700
That’s the conservation of energy.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:51.500
In any practical sense, all that really matters
is what the energy does.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.880
That’s what work is!

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:57.440
So let’s put it this way:
Energy is the amount of stuff you CAN do.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.420
Work is the amount of stuff you HAVE done
or WILL do.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:02.480
That’s it.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:03.980
But what do you mean by “stuff”?

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:07.480
I mean anything that could exist or happen.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:14.520
Lifting, Swimming, Climbing, Dancing, Swinging,
Waving, Running, Slithering

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.560
Uh, doing other things

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:22.080
Boiling, Lighting, Chemical Reactions, Nuclear Explosions

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.380
or the very existence of matter itself.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:25.860
Well, that escalated quickly.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.280
Ok, now back to magnets.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:31.920
If we want to know if magnets can do work,
we just need an example of them doing stuff.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:32.620
Boom!

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:34.160
Magnets doing stuff!

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.680
Guess my work is done here.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:36.860
Thanks for liking and sharing.

00:01:36.869 --> 00:01:37.869
Hold on a second!

00:01:37.869 --> 00:01:42.020
I was reading in this electrodynamics book
that it’s not actually the magnet doing

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:43.060
the work.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:46.439
Just because it’s in a book, it doesn’t
make it true.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.569
When textbooks say magnetic force can’t
do work, they have to do this convoluted

00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:51.660
dance around it.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:55.200
Kind of like this:
While it may appear that the magnets are doing work,

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.680
it is really just the electrons in the
magnet doing the work.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.300
No!

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:04.259
Regardless of what objects or particles are
doing the work, they will be doing that work

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:05.380
through a force.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:09.900
Work is always done by a force in the direction
of a displacement.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:13.080
That’s how we get units of newton meters
or foot pounds.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.500
There is always a force.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.960
So, where do the textbooks get the idea?

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.720
The innately human desire for very simple
rules.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:21.870
The argument goes a little something like
this:

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:24.150
Imagine there’s a proton moving to the right.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:27.920
Suddenly, a magnetic field is turned on directed
into your screen.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:33.010
The right-hand rule tells us the magnetic
force on that proton will be upward perpendicular

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:35.040
to the direction the proton is moving.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:39.760
In fact, this cross-product means the magnetic
force will always be perpendicular to that

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:40.440
motion.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:45.140
Since work is only done along the direction
of motion, magnetic force can’t do it.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:49.100
It seems like a solid argument until you stop and think about it.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:54.240
Yes, the magnetic force on this proton in
this specific case isn’t doing any work.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.460
All it did was change the path of that proton
from straight to circular.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:03.340
However, with attracting magnets, there is
definitely a magnetic force and that force

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:06.430
is definitely along the direction the magnets
move.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:08.380
That magnetic force is doing work.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:11.240
Maybe those are two different kinds of magnetic
forces.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:14.040
They’re not, but I’ll give you a couple
more examples anyway.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:18.920
Let’s say you replace that proton with a
wire carrying an electric current to the right.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:23.040
That current will have an upward magnetic
force on it just like the proton did,

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.840
but the current can’t go in a circle.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:28.620
It’s bound to the wire, so the wire will
just move straight upward.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:32.860
That’s a force in the direction the wire
is moving, which means work is being done

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:33.740
on the wire.

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:34.960
Let’s go even deeper!

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:36.230
Remember that proton?!

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:39.700
The upward magnetic force we found earlier
is not the whole story.

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:41.820
Protons do a lot more than just move.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:46.240
They also have another property called Quantum
Spin that can turn a particle like a proton

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.640
or electron into a tiny magnet.

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:51.920
That tiny magnet can also respond to the magnetic
field

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:55.520
causing another magnetic force that can do
work on that proton.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:04:01.380
In fact, that’s all a permanent magnet is:
A pile of lined-up electrons acting as tiny

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:05.240
magnets, held in place by a bunch of protons
and other electrons.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:07.900
That’s exactly how these magnets do work.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:11.240
That precious simple rule is turning out to
be more like this:

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:14.680
Magnetic force can’t do work
on a single charged particle

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.750
assuming you ignore the particle’s spin.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:20.370
It’s kind of like that English rule: I before
E except after C

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:24.000
unless you’re a weird beige foreign neighbor
running a feisty heist.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.240
With that many exceptions, is it really a
rule anymore?

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.160
So, are you satisfied with this answer?

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.420
Let me know down in the comments.

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:31.960
Thanks for liking and sharing this video.

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:36.690
A special thank you goes out to Patreon patrons
like Rick Finn who are literally making my

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:39.400
life possible right now. Thank you so much!

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.840
And until next time, remember, it’s ok to
be a little crazy.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:46.620
The featured comment comes from Bobby Harper who
